<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Islam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Muslim, Muslims, Islamic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Islam is a monotheistic religion founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> in the seventh century CE through the teaching of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quran">Quran</a>. It shaped the founding and governance of many empires, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun</a>, Umayyad and Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphates</a> to the Ottoman, Safavid and Mughal empires. It also spread through trade and conquest to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>, where it shaped states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
